    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-17T21:27:35+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-17T21:27:35+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-17T10:57:35Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-17T10:57:35Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred south of the Bight, extends a ridge of high pressure over most of South Australia. The high and ridge will move slowly eastwards during the week to be in the Tasman Sea on Thursday. A low pressure system and associated trough over Western Australia will move over South Australia mid to late in the week. Another high pressure system follows and moves over South Australia on Saturday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-17T21:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-18T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-17T10:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-17T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of rain north of Coober Pedy, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy. Thunderstorms possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding in the far west. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-18T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-19T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-17T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-18T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Very high chance of showers west of Coober Pedy, medium chance elsewhere. A thunderstorm likely. Thunderstorms possibly severe with damaging winds, locally destructive, giant and large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending north to northeasterly 25 to 40 km/h during the morning then tending northwest to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 17 and 21 with daytime temperatures reaching 27 to 36.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 5:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-19T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-18T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers east of Coober Pedy, medium chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm, possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding. Winds north to northwesterly 20 to 30 km/h tending west to northwesterly 25 to 35 km/h in the early afternoon then tending northwest to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h in the late evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 17 and 22 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-20T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-19T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">The chance of a thunderstorm east of Stuart Highway in the morning. Mostly sunny day. Winds south to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h tending west to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the day then tending southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 21 with daytime temperatures reaching 30 to 35.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-11-21T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-22T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-20T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-21T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending north to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h during the morning then tending north to northwesterly during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 21 with daytime temperatures reaching around 40.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
